  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ricemmkg#Leaf_Sheath_Lesion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ricemmkg#Symptom"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">leaf sheath lesion</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Oval or ellipsoidal greenish-grey lesions on the leaf sheath, initially just above the soil or water level, later grey-white with brown margins, as described for sheath blight in the IRRI Rice Knowledge Bank fact sheet (accessed 2026-09-15). Labelled "Stem Rot Symptom" until 0.7.0-dev: stem rot is a separate rice disease whose early lesions on the outer leaf sheath resemble these. Its IRI was Stem_Rot_Symptom until 0.7.0-dev; it was renamed together with the move to the w3id namespace, before any term had been published under that namespace, so no deprecation was needed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rice:affectsPlantPart rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ricemmkg#Leaf_Sheath"/>
  </rdf:Description>
